# Read from the build context, which `docker-compose.yml` sets to `./apps/api`. Same
# reason as the web one: a `.dockerignore` at the repo root would be read by nothing.

# 87 of this context's 91 MB, and both are the host's own toolchain rather than input.
# The Dockerfile runs its own `./gradlew clean bootJar` inside a linux JDK image, so a
# darwin `build/` and a warm host `.gradle/` are weight that could only mislead it.
# `build` matches the directory and not `build.gradle.kts`, which the Dockerfile needs.
build
.gradle
.kotlin

# The generated AES key for the secrets the setup wizard stores. It belongs to the
# machine and to the `kanso-data` volume, never to an image layer.
data

.git
.claude
